course: dictionary
lesson: 1840
title: Reading clues about cochineal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cochineal can mean a red dye, or the tiny insect that makes it. Context helps you tell which. «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs that live on cactus» tells you cochineal is a kind of bug, and that the bugs are crushed to make red colour.
explain: The sentence gives more clues: the bugs live on cactus, and the colour is used in sweets, yoghurt and lipstick. So cochineal is a red dye, and the bugs are where it comes from. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: The sentence also says «the Aztecs used it to dye cloth», so the word it must mean a colour that can be used on cloth. Context gives you strong clues, and a dictionary confirms them.
fact: Cochineal is a deep red dye made from tiny scale insects.
fact: These insects live on prickly pear cacti.
fact: Cochineal colours food, drinks, make-up and cloth.
fact: The Aztecs prized cochineal, and later the Spanish shipped it to Europe.
fact: It coloured British soldiers' red coats, and on food labels it can appear as carmine or E120.
exercise: «The red food colour carmine is made from crushed cochineal bugs.» What are cochineal bugs? | Lipstick shades | A type of cactus | *Tiny insects that give a red dye | Red sweets made from cactus
exercise: What is another name for cochineal on a food label? | Prickly pear | Cactus | *Carmine | Vinegar
exercise: Why is cochineal not vegetarian? | *It comes from insects | It is a plant | It is made from fruit | It is grown in soil
test: «The Aztecs used cochineal to dye cloth.» What does dye mean here? | To cook something | *To colour something | To cut something | To wash something
test: What do cochineal insects live on? | Oak trees | Rivers | Grass | *Prickly pear cacti
exam: In «crushed cochineal bugs», which word tells you cochineal means the insect itself? | Cactus | *Bugs | Crushed | Red
